{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/778932-seelie-redcaps-how-to-distinguish-them-from-trolls","id":778932,"title":"Seelie Redcaps; how to distinguish them from Trolls?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-03T05:33:18-08:00","id":778932,"title":"Seelie Redcaps; how to distinguish them from Trolls?","content":"their rare, sure, but a lot of the descriptions ive seen makes it sound like they act like trolls, with a dash of Drizzt for good Measure...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T07:33:46-08:00","id":778998,"title":"","content":"They have bad attitudes and still occasionally eat what they ought not to, whereas most trolls don't. It's a good cop, bad cop kind of setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T08:42:18-08:00","id":779030,"title":"","content":"Trolls are &quot;civilized warrior&quot; archetypes: knights, musketeers, soldiers and noble prize-fighters.<br /> <br /> Redcaps are &quot;uncivilized savage&quot; archetypes: orcs, woodsmen, barbarians, big bad wolves.<br /> <br /> You can have unseelie Trolls that are black knights, seedy mercenaries, and brutal &quot;anything for a win&quot; prize-fighters, and you can have seelie Redcaps that are &quot;noble savage Indians,&quot; rough-hewn guides, and thugs with hearts of gold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T10:44:10-08:00","id":779079,"title":"","content":"Plus they look different. Even the chivalrous redcaps are likely to be considered intimidating, only they'll appear more like bouncers and film noir detectives than the marauders and hired goons you'd find among the Unseelie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:07:38-08:00","id":779097,"title":"","content":"According to the redcap kithbook, Seelie redcaps tend to come in two kinds: the jokes, who try to make themselves seem harmless to be accepted, and the badasses, who turn the primal hunger of the redcaps towards Seelie ends. The badasses practice self-mastery, knowing when to keep their primal drives under control and when to let them out.<br /> <br /> Trolls, however, are coming from a very different place. For them, honour is a source of strength - with great responsibility comes great power. It empowers them as it binds them.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, Seelie redcaps are about self-control, in one form or another. Trolls are about duty and responsibility. One looks inside, the other outside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T21:01:26-08:00","id":779518,"title":"","content":"Trolls protect. They are as the stones. They are as the Mountains. They are s the great Oaks. Red Caps are Fire and Storm! Trolls are Shields. Red Caps are Swords. Or simply put a Troll's strength is Defending others. a Redcap's strength is Destroying Others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}